  "_comment": "🧩️ Ticket 26/09/02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION: split out of the former `✳️any` catch-all. ASPRS LAS 1.0 §2.3 (Variable Length Record Header/Data) is a normatively distinct region of the file (a keyed list of typed metadata blocks living between the Public Header Block and the point data), so `insert-vlr`/`remove-vlr`/`set-vlr-data` are owned here rather than by `✳️header`. The leaf struct definitions physically moved into this subset's own `🧬️schema/🧬️mutations`; the `LasMutation` enum, its `apply`/diff dispatch and the real binary codec they compile into remain in `✳️header` (the whole-file reader/writer is one shared, always-co-resident implementation across every LAS region -- moving it would duplicate ~800 lines of codec per subset for a format that, unlike PDF/A or STEP's conformance classes, has no alternate standalone document profile to justify it; same family-module reuse this repo already uses for svg tiny/basic). This subset owns no new third-party oracle: `las-1-0-any-mutate` (declared by `../../✳️header/🧪️oracle/🔣️.json`, merged into the shared registry) already reads back every VLR field through the SAME independent `las` crate reader used for the header/points mutations.",
